---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const tools = [
  {
    href: '/tools/impermanent-loss-calculator/',
    eyebrow: 'Divergence against holding',
    title: 'Impermanent Loss Calculator',
    description: 'Compare 50/50, weighted, and concentrated range scenarios, chart the IL curve, and share the exact inputs by URL.',
    status: 'Runs in your browser'
  },
  {
    href: '/tools/lp-profit-calculator/',
    eyebrow: 'Net result on one ledger',
    title: 'LP Profit & Return Calculator',
    description: 'Fee income, divergence and gas resolved into one net figure, benchmarked against holding the assets you deposited rather than against cash.',
    status: 'Runs in your browser'
  },
  {
    href: '/tools/uniswap-v3-liquidity-calculator/',
    eyebrow: 'Bounded price ranges',
    title: 'Uniswap v3 & Concentrated Liquidity Calculator',
    description: 'Set a price range and a deposit. Returns token composition at every price, capital efficiency against a full-range position, estimated fees and the result against holding.',
    status: 'Runs in your browser'
  },
  {
    href: '/tools/liquidity-pool-calculator/',
    eyebrow: 'Fee and incentive APR',
    title: 'Liquidity Pool Fees, Rewards & APR Calculator',
    description: 'Model trading-fee APR and incentive APR separately, then combine them with time in range and gas.',
    status: 'Runs in your browser'
  },
  {
    href: '/tools/meteora-dlmm-calculator/',
    eyebrow: 'Discrete bins on Solana',
    title: 'Meteora DLMM Calculator',
    description: 'Model discrete bin prices, Spot, Curve and Bid-Ask shapes, dynamic fees, range state and divergence against holding.',
    status: 'Runs in your browser'
  }
];

const frameworks = [
  { href: '/guides/liquidity-pool-research-checklist/', title: 'Pool due diligence checklist', description: 'The pre-deposit questions, in the order a research desk asks them.' },
  { href: '/guides/how-to-evaluate-a-liquidity-pool/', title: 'Five-part evaluation framework', description: 'Structure for assessing invariant, depth, incentives, security and execution.' },
  { href: '/guides/onchain-liquidity-metrics/', title: 'Onchain metrics reference', description: 'Which measurements matter, where to read them, and how each one misleads.' }
];

const collectionSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  name: 'DeFi Liquidity Tools — LiquidityPools.app',
  url: 'https://liquiditypools.app/tools/',
  description: 'Free calculators and research frameworks for liquidity providers: impermanent loss, fee yield, pool due diligence.',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'ItemList',
    numberOfItems: tools.length,
    itemListElement: tools.map((tool, index) => ({
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: index + 1,
      name: tool.title,
      url: `https://liquiditypools.app${tool.href}`
    }))
  }
};
const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://liquiditypools.app/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Tools', item: 'https://liquiditypools.app/tools/' }
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout title="Liquidity Pool Tools & Calculators — LiquidityPools.app" description="Free liquidity pool calculators: impermanent loss, fee yield and APR modelling, plus the research frameworks behind them. No wallet connection, nothing stored.">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(collectionSchema)} />
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Calculators</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Five calculators with published formulas.</h1>
      <p>Each one answers a single question and states its formula and its limits on the same page. Inputs stay in your browser: no wallet connection, nothing stored.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button--line" href="/methodology/">Read the methodology and test vectors</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><div class="kicker">Calculators</div><h2 class="section-title">Model the position before you fund it.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-intro">Each tool states its assumptions and links to the guide that derives them. A number without its model is not a result.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="article-grid article-grid--two">
        {tools.map((tool) => (
          <a class="tool-card" href={tool.href}>
            <div class="tool-card__eyebrow">{tool.eyebrow}</div>
            <h3>{tool.title}</h3>
            <p>{tool.description}</p>
            <span class="tool-card__status">{tool.status}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--ink">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">Frameworks</div><h2 class="section-title">Checklists that do not need a calculator.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/">Browse all guides</a></div>
      <div class="track-grid track-grid--three">
        {frameworks.map((item, index) => (
          <a class="track" href={item.href}>
            <span class="track__number">Framework {index + 1}</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.description}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--mist">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="guide-layout">
        <aside class="guide-aside">
          <h2>On this page</h2>
          <a href="#method">Method</a>
          <a href="/guides/impermanent-loss-formula/">IL formula</a>
          <a href="/guides/lp-fees-vs-impermanent-loss/">Break-even model</a>
        </aside>
        <div class="article-content">
          <h2 id="method">How these tools are built</h2>
          <p>Every calculator here implements a published formula, states the inputs it needs in plain terms, and lists what it deliberately excludes. The shared <a href="/methodology/">calculator methodology</a> publishes the formulas and the exact worked vectors used by the automated tests.</p>
          <p>The concentrated-liquidity calculator implements bounded position mathematics shared by Uniswap v3-style pools. Meteora has a separate calculator because DLMM uses fixed-price, constant-sum bins and a protocol-specific dynamic-fee formula. The impermanent loss calculator covers full-range weighted pools and bounded scenarios. The fee calculator keeps trading fees and token incentives separate, while the LP return calculator combines observed income and costs against holding. None predicts the future or substitutes for reading a pool's current state.</p>

          <h2 id="trackers">What we do not build</h2>
          <p>There is no liquidity pool tracker or LP position tracker here, and there will not be one until it can be built on live data we control. A DeFi liquidity tracker that reports stale or partial position state is worse than no tracker at all, because it invites decisions on numbers nobody verified.</p>
          <p>For live position tracking today, reconstruct positions on Revert Finance, read pool state directly from a block explorer, and use pool analytics on Dune or DeFiLlama for volume and fee history. The frameworks in <a href="/guides/onchain-liquidity-metrics/">Onchain Liquidity Metrics</a> and <a href="/guides/token-liquidity-analysis/">Token Liquidity Analysis</a> explain which measurements to take from those sources and how each one misleads.</p>
          <p>For the reasoning behind each model, start with <a href="/guides/impermanent-loss-formula/">The Impermanent Loss Formula</a> and <a href="/guides/lp-fees-vs-impermanent-loss/">LP Fees vs Impermanent Loss</a>. To verify a live position against onchain data rather than a model, reconstruct it on Revert Finance and compare the two.</p>
          <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
          <p>Every model on these pages is built from published specifications and research rather than from house rules. The primary sources are:</p>
          <ol class="tool-sources">
            <li><a href="https://uniswap.org/whitepaper-v3.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Uniswap v3 Core Whitepaper (Adams et al., 2021)</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.06046" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Automated Market Making and Loss-Versus-Rebalancing (Milionis et al., 2022)</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.12732" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SoK: Decentralized Exchanges with Automated Market Maker Protocols (Xu et al., 2021)</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.bis.org/publ/bisbull58.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Miners as intermediaries: extractable value and market manipulation in crypto and DeFi (BIS Bulletin No 58, 2022)</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.uniswap.org/hc/en-us/articles/37113550065549-What-are-the-risks-when-providing-liquidity" target="_blank" rel="noopener">What are the risks when providing liquidity? (Uniswap Labs)</a></li>
          </ol>

        </div>
        <aside class="guide-aside">
          <h2>Editorial note</h2>
          <p>These tools are educational. They are not investment, legal, tax or financial advice, and they make no claim about the future performance of any pool.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
